.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-IMPROVE" 1  "skogai runner-improve 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-improve \- ask an agent to edit files, print the patch. pure unless \-\-apply
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner improve\fR [OPTIONS] [REQUEST]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
ask an agent to edit files, print the patch. pure unless \-\-apply
.br

.br
the agent returns whole files (schema `edit`), the patch is derived
.br
here with `diff \-u`, so a bad hunk header can never break it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR=[\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
files to hand over, default this module's argc.sh and module.md
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR=\fIMODEL\fR
.br
model, default runner.model
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
.br
apply the patch to the tree
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
[\fIREQUEST\fR]...
.br
what to change; options go before it, everything after is the request
